&lt;h2 id="about-me"&gt;About Me&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class="homepage-about-logos" aria-label="Affiliations"&gt;
&lt;a href="https://www.lamda.nju.edu.cn/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-label="LAMDA Group"&gt;
&lt;img src="https://mingyang1010.github.io/img/lamda_logo.png" alt="LAMDA Group" /&gt;
&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;a href="https://www.nju.edu.cn/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-label="Nanjing University"&gt;
&lt;img src="https://mingyang1010.github.io/img/nju_logo.png" alt="Nanjing University" /&gt;
&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I am Ming Yang (杨铭), a first-year Ph.D. student in the M.S.-Ph.D. track at the &lt;a class="link" href="http://ai.nju.edu.cn/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
&gt;School of Artificial Intelligence&lt;/a&gt; of &lt;a class="link" href="https://www.nju.edu.cn/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
&gt;Nanjing University&lt;/a&gt;, advised by Professor &lt;a class="link" href="https://cs.nju.edu.cn/liyf/index.htm" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
&gt;Yu-Feng Li (李宇峰)&lt;/a&gt;, and a member of the &lt;a class="link" href="https://www.lamda.nju.edu.cn/CH.MainPage.ashx" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
&gt;LAMDA Group (机器学习与数据挖掘研究所)&lt;/a&gt;, led by Professor &lt;a class="link" href="https://cs.nju.edu.cn/zhouzh/index.htm" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
&gt;Zhi-Hua Zhou (周志华)&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="biography"&gt;Biography
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;div class="biography-list"&gt;
&lt;div class="biography-row"&gt;
&lt;span&gt;2024.09 - Present&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span&gt;M.S.-Ph.D. Program in Artificial Intelligence, Nanjing University (Ph.D. stage from 2026.09)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class="biography-row"&gt;
&lt;span&gt;2020.09 - 2024.06&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span&gt;B.Sc. in Computer Science and Technology, Nanjing University of Aeronautics and Astronautics&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h2 id="research-interests"&gt;Research Interests
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;My research focuses on reliable multimodal intelligence, particularly reasoning, planning, and test-time adaptation. I also explore neuro-symbolic methods and agentic foundation models for remote sensing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="academic-service"&gt;Academic Service
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Conference Reviewer:&lt;/strong&gt; ICLR 2025; ICML 2025, 2026; KDD 2025; IJCAI 2025, 2026; ACML 2026.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Links</title><link>https://mingyang1010.github.io/links/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://mingyang1010.github.io/links/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;To use this feature, add &lt;code&gt;links&lt;/code&gt; section to frontmatter.&lt;/p&gt;
